hexagon: stream the rows of GDN_CONV_CHUNK through VTCM with the DMA

The cost

GDN_CONV_CHUNK reads each token row of the projection with vector loads
from DDR through the L2, and it writes each output row the same way. On
the phone (HTP0, Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0, one prefill ubatch of 1024 tokens) the op
takes 71 ms of the 1044 ms of the ubatch, at 11.5 GB/s. The PMU stage of
2026-09-24 gives the cause: the HVX loads from L2 are 79 % of the HVX
stalls of the op, and the op does not use the DMA.

The change

The threads get whole 64-channel units of the channels. For each block of
36 tokens, one 2D DMA transfer moves the channels of a thread from each
token row into VTCM. The bands of the packed path compute from VTCM into
VTCM with aligned loads and stores, and one 2D DMA transfer writes the
block to the output. Two buffers of each kind let the transfers of the next
block and of the block before run while the bands compute. When the
channel count has an odd 32-channel block, the last thread gets it as a
padded unit, thus each channel takes the packed path.

GGML_HEXAGON_GDN_CONV_DMA=0 keeps the path without the DMA. The preset
value is 1. The host gives the value to the DSP in the kernel params of
each op (htp/htp-gdn-params.h), thus an A/B run needs no other build.
test-backend-ops gets the conv chain at the 4B shape (8192 channels, 512
tokens) and at an odd channel count (8224 channels, 2 snapshot slots). The
conv chain of a batch on the HTP backend gets the bound 1e-6 in place of
1e-7: GDN_CONV_CHUNK rounds the tokens and the state to f16, and the phone
gives an NMSE of 3.0e-07 to 3.3e-07 with the kernel of the series before
this patch (6144 to 8224 channels, 100 to 512 tokens, stage gdnk of
2026-09-24). The DMA path takes every channel through that f16 path, thus
64 and 96 channels give 1.4e-07 where the path without the DMA gives an
exact f32 result for them.

The results

The kernel lab (tools/htp-lab, target gdnconvdma, the v79 timing model,
8192 channels, 288 tokens, 6 threads): the path without the DMA takes
1597110 cycles, which is 64.5 ms for 24 layers of 1024 tokens. The DMA path
takes 858131 cycles (34.7 ms) when the lab does not count the transfers,
thus that is its compute. The bytes of the op (32 MiB in and 32 MiB out for
each layer of 1024 tokens) need about 29 ms at 55 GB/s. The functional run
against the scalar reference passes for 8192 channels and 76 tokens, 8224
channels and 40 tokens with 3 snapshot slots, and 64 channels and 7 tokens
with 3 slots: NMSE 2.9e-07 to 3.3e-07, and each snapshot slot is exact.

The phone stage gdnk of 2026-09-25 (HTP0, Qwen3.5-4B Q8_0) runs one build
of the series with four switch settings. Variant A is the kernels before
the series, and variant B adds this patch. In one prefill ubatch of 1024
tokens, GDN_CONV_CHUNK takes 33.2 ms of DSP op time in place of 73.4 ms
(the median of 6 graphs). tg32 gives 10.70 t/s for B and 10.69 t/s for A.
The runner rejected two of the three pp512 rounds of B for a change of the
CPU caps. The round that stays gives 1025.8 t/s, and A gives 1005.5 to
1023.8 t/s. test-backend-ops passes the 82 cases of the gated delta net
ops with the whole series, and the 17 conv chain cases are part of them.

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 with the patches of patches/series above this one.

